{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c567","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07039-8c36-7981-972e-5e4ed62aa495"},"sequence":270,"recorded_at":1780531400000535,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"ee3bfad3-4220-425d-83ef-438f4f623084"},"task_id":"ee3bfad3-4220-425d-83ef-438f4f623084","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"ee3bfad3-4220-425d-83ef-438f4f623084","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev6/README.txt`.\n1|TASK-260830-32jeti round-6 review probe pack.\n2|Measured at candidate tree aa190969ba39fee5234fbb10bbff2af68441c5a0.\n3|\n4|Harness (from the round-5 pack, unchanged):\n5|  mutate.py            plant one mutant, run, cp-restore, sha256-verify\n6|  repeat.py            run a spec N times and tally results (map-iteration rule)\n7|                       usage: python3 repeat.py <spec>.json <reps>\n8|\n9|F1 — switch-shaped closed vocabularies the census cannot see:\n10|  census.json          C1..C7  (C1, C2 SURVIVE = the finding; C3..C7 kill the census itself)\n11|  census2.json         C8..C10 (C8 SURVIVES = the finding; C9 proves build-tagged files are scanned)\n12|  stability.json       C1/C2/C8 for repeat.py; observed 12/12, 12/12, 22/24 SURVIVED\n13|  c8only.json          C8 alone, for characterising its nondeterministic \"kill\"\n14|  census_probe.json    C1/C2/C8 run against the probe fixture below; all three KILLED,\n15|                       which is what proves the widenings are real acceptances\n16|\n17|  review-round6-switch-vocab-probe_test.go.txt\n18|                       drop in as internal/provhost/zz_reviewprobe_test.go.\n19|                       Shipped tree: all three REFUSE. With the matching mutant: ACCEPT.\n20|\n21|  enum_vars.go         independent denominator: AST walk of every package-level\n22|                       var/const/type in the 15 non-test files.\n23|                       usage: go run enum_vars.go ./internal/provhost\n24|\n25|F2 — ExecRunner discards a judged result on a stdin EPIPE:\n26|  review-round6-runner-race-probe_test.go.txt\n27|                       drop in as internal/provhost/zz_runnerrace_test.go.\n28|                       Observed across two runs:\n29|                         valid frame discarded   10/400 and 2/300\n30|                         crash misclassified     32/400 and 6/300\n31|\n32|G-B replay (round-5 pack, unchanged; results in the verdict):\n33|  r4/b1 b1b b2 b2r b3 b4 b5 b6 b7   122 rows -> 120 killed, 2 stated bounds\n34|  probe_widen.json                   14 rows -> 12 killed, R1/R3 stated bounds\n35|  probe_failclosed.json               4 rows -> 4 killed\n36|  k6fix.json                          1 row  -> killed"}}}
