{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07039-8c36-7981-972e-5e4ed62aa495"},"sequence":571,"recorded_at":1780531400001137,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"755e8d3a-314d-4bd9-8eb6-b2cf6902f62f"},"task_id":"755e8d3a-314d-4bd9-8eb6-b2cf6902f62f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"755e8d3a-314d-4bd9-8eb6-b2cf6902f62f","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-18-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"standard\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.md | sed -n 1,20p; echo ===; sed -n 3390,3440p internal/specdoc/SPEC.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Find profile vocabulary in spec section 7.7\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"612:The persisted profile enum is <code>standard</code> or <code>yolo</code>.\\n661:| <code>PROFILE-PI-EQUAL-MAPPING</code> | Pi changes <code>standard</code> to <code>yolo</code> at E1 while both map to <code>default_unrestricted_tool_set</code> | Ax still persists and reports P1/E1; equal provider argv text is not authority to erase E1 |\\n1477:| <code>execution_profile</code> | enum | <code>standard</code> or <code>yolo</code> |\\n1588:  \\\"execution_profile\\\": \\\"standard\\\",\\n1772:| <code>provider.launched</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code> |\\n1779:| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code> |\\n1785:| <code>fork.created</code> | <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>new_session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>provider_fork_mode:native&#124;supported_import&#124;task_board_clone</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>source_profile_event_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\\n1786:| <code>profile.changed</code> | <code>from:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>to:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>confirmed:boolean</code> |\\n1790:| <code>task_board.launched</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code>, <code>state:running&#124;idle</code> |\\n1872:| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\\n3074:| <code>launch</code> | <code>{session_record:Session Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, launch_plan:Launch Plan, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\\n3083:| <code>resume</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\\n3084:| <code>fork</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, source_identity:Provider Identity Record, source_checkpoint:Checkpoint Record, new_session_record:Session Record, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, result_kind:native_fork&#124;supported_import, planned_native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null, spawn_plan:SpawnPlan, requires_provider_materialization:boolean, provenance_verified:boolean}</code> |\\n3438:<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior\\n3440:alias that silently expands to unrestricted mode. Provider-specific standard\\n3971:task-board session resume --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --ax-session SESSION_ID --lease-epoch EPOCH --lease-id LEASE_ID --profile standard|yolo --json\\n4083:| <code>launch</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4, provider_id:provider-id, launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt, task_element_id:string[1..128], board:Board Identity, board_goal:Board Goal&#124;null, native_goal_binding:bound&#124;prompt&#124;none, profile:standard&#124;yolo, launch_plan:BridgeLaunchPlan, workspace_paths:map(UUIDv7,absolute-path)[1..256]}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, manager_session_ref:string[1..512], provider_id:provider-id, provider_version:string[1..128], native_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null, launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt, state:running&#124;idle, input_enabled:boolean, ax_binding:BridgeBinding, capabilities:sorted unique launch&#124;status&#124;export&#124;import&#124;open&#124;adopt&#124;stop&#124;resume[8..8], native_goal_binding:bound&#124;prompt&#124;none}</code> |\\n4090:| <code>resume</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,manager_session_ref:string[1..512],ax_session_id:UUIDv7,lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0,lease_id:UUIDv4,profile:standard&#124;yolo}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, manager_session_ref:string[1..512], ax_binding:BridgeBinding, native_session_ref:string[1..512], process_started:boolean, state:running&#124;idle}</code> |\\n4111:  \\\"profile\\\": \\\"standard\\\",\\n4377:<code>standard|yolo</code>; <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is a digest or\\n===\\n    \\\"extensions\\\": {}\\n  }\\n}\\n~~~\\n\\n### 7.6 Quiescence proof\\n\\nA successful <code>quiesce</code> response MUST contain:\\n\\n- provider ID and exact version;\\n- <code>input_blocked = true</code>;\\n- a provider-specific terminal/idle event reference;\\n- <code>foreground_idle = true</code>;\\n- <code>background_idle = true</code> when the provider can prove it;\\n- open child process and open durable-database handle counts, both zero;\\n- the last stable provider-store digest or metadata generation; and\\n- <code>safe = true</code>.\\n\\nIf background idleness, process exit, or store closure cannot be proven,\\n<code>safe</code> MUST be false and graceful takeover MUST stop. A force\\ntakeover is a separate operator action; the plugin MUST NOT silently convert the\\nrequest.\\n\\nFor a safe direct-provider proof, Checkpoint Safe Boundary Evidence copies\\nprovider ID/version, input/idle booleans, and maps\\n<code>open_child_count</code> to <code>open_processes</code> and\\n<code>open_database_handle_count</code> to\\n<code>open_database_handles</code>; <code>evidence</code> is the accepted\\nadapter mechanism (<code>provider_api</code>, <code>provider_event</code>,\\n<code>managed_pty</code>, or <code>accepted_test</code>). RPC\\n<code>SafeBoundary</code> additionally copies the boundary reference and store\\ngeneration, sets <code>store_stable = true</code>, and normalizes\\n<code>child_process_open</code> to <code>process_open</code>. No other lossy or\\nprovider-defined mapping is permitted.\\n\\n### 7.7 Profile mapping\\n\\nThe v0.3.0 <code>yolo</code> mappings are:\\n\\n| Provider | Required adapter mapping |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Codex | <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> (alias <code>--yolo</code> is accepted by current CLI but the long form SHOULD be persisted in diagnostics) |\\n| Claude | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\\n| Gemini CLI | <code>--approval-mode=yolo</code> |\\n| Muse | <code>--yolo</code> |\\n| Antigravity | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\\n| Pi 0.73.1 | No invented flag; use the provider's default full built-in tool set and report <code>profile_mapping = \\\"default_unrestricted_tool_set\\\"</code> |\\n\\n<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior\\nand MUST omit every unrestricted flag above. It MUST NOT reuse a machine-local\\nalias that silently expands to unrestricted mode. Provider-specific standard\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7598,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1900,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
