{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c899","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07039-8c36-7981-972e-5e4ed62aa495"},"sequence":679,"recorded_at":1780531400001353,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a07596a1-3e43-42de-9cb0-1c66d25ba29c"},"task_id":"a07596a1-3e43-42de-9cb0-1c66d25ba29c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a07596a1-3e43-42de-9cb0-1c66d25ba29c","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-24-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"Stated bounds\\\" -A 40 internal/provhost/doc.go | head -60; echo ===LOGBOOK===; grep -n \\\"15/15\\\\|0926\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head; wc -l LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read doc bounds and logbook entries\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"44:// Stated bounds: stderr capture is capped at 1 MiB (an implementation\\n45-// resource bound, not a protocol limit); error details carry the failure\\n46-// class, member names, and the observed version string only — never\\n47-// environment or stderr content. Mutation receipts live in the\\n48-// provider transaction document and the plugin, not in the host: the\\n49-// host holds no cross-call cache, so cross-crash durability of\\n50-// (operation, operation_id) results is the document's property, and\\n51-// the host side pins the sole key shape, byte-identical retry bytes,\\n52-// and the mismatch surface. The Section 8 provider/platform cell\\n53-// values are evidence labels, not host behavior: the host pins the\\n54-// fail-closed direction (conditional, unsupported, and unknown are\\n55-// never usable) for every capability-by-status tuple rather than one\\n56-// cell value. Section 8.2 store-exclusion roots and the remaining\\n57-// Section 7.5 request vocabularies have no host production yet.\\n58-package provhost\\n===LOGBOOK===\\n8:### 0926 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-6 rework: the vocabulary class closed by census\\n12:- EVIDENCE: probe_widen.json replay, full-package runs, cp+sha256 restores: W1–W9 KILLED (each red three ways — derivation, census subtest, entry-point refusal row), W10/R2/R4 killed, R1/R3 survive as the stated behaviour-preserving bounds. Fail-closed attacks all red: wrong type name, bad cell marker, off-table identity window, unregistered planted vocabulary (`has no registered spec derivation`), blinded string-map scan (`names no production vocabulary`), dropped registration. `requireVocabulary` now uses reflect.DeepEqual, so the V4 joined-member mutant is killed by the derivation alone. Gates: build/vet/GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` 15/15 green, provhost -race green, provhost cover 86.5% unchanged.\\n27:- EVIDENCE: 29-mutant replay (the 28 real survivors plus MA8) with the reviewer's own harness and spec files: 29 killed, 0 survived. `go build`, `go vet`, `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 15/15 green, provhost `-race` green, provhost cover 86.4% → 86.5%.\\n55:- EVIDENCE: 19-mutant verify sweep (`/tmp/rev2-verify.sh`, cp-aside/cp-back per mutant, presence asserted, restore byte-verified): 18 killed, 1 declared equivalent (M09b). True two-site R17 verified killed separately with the reviewer's exact flip. `go test ./...` exit 0 (15/15), `-race` on provhost exit 0, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt gate clean, `go build` on linux/windows exit 0, `tracecheck` exit 0 unchanged (17/403, 74 cases). provhost cover 86.1% → 88.1%.\\n68:- EVIDENCE: 25 narrowing mutants, each verified present, compiling, and restored — 25 killed, 0 survivors. `go test ./...` exit 0 (15/15), `-race` exit 0 in batches over all 15, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `gofmt` clean, `tracecheck` exit 0, catalog generate current.\\n     783 LOGBOOK.md\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2973,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 744,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
