on source for package-level []string/map[string]bool/map[string]string with membership use (unknownMember argument, map index, range operand) and requires each of the 19 found vocabularies to carry an executing derivation, in both directions.\n12|- EVIDENCE: probe_widen.json replay, full-package runs, cp+sha256 restores: W1–W9 KILLED (each red three ways — derivation, census subtest, entry-point refusal row), W10/R2/R4 killed, R1/R3 survive as the stated behaviour-preserving bounds. Fail-closed attacks all red: wrong type name, bad cell marker, off-table identity window, unregistered planted vocabulary (`has no registered spec derivation`), blinded string-map scan (`names no production vocabulary`), dropped registration. `requireVocabulary` now uses reflect.DeepEqual, so the V4 joined-member mutant is killed by the derivation alone. Gates: build/vet/GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` 15/15 green, provhost -race green, provhost cover 86.5% unchanged.\n13|- ANOMALY: the capability-value sentence shares its window with the warnings sentence, so a naive span read derives five members including warnings; the derivation truncates to the declaring sentence. The bare 5.5 closed sentence repeats in four sections, so the identity quote carries its schema opener to stay unique. The *Required order lists are excluded from the census by construction (missingMember-only use), which is what keeps R1/R3 surviving.\n14|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n15|\n16|### 0830 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-5 rework: the 28 real survivors, closed by derivation\n17|\n18|- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-4 verdict (changes requested, 106 mutants, 76 killed, 30 survived, 2 stated bounds, 28 real). Test-only rework in `internal/provhost` plus one comment restatement; production untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n19|- FIX (F1, blocking): the eight closed vocabularies the three existing specdoc derivations did not cover are now derived the same way in `internal/provhost/closed_vocabularies_test.go` — probe statuses and evidence from the Section 7.4 sentences, architectures from 7.4 prose cross-checked against the 7.5 probe request row, probe platforms from that row (sorted both sides: the row lists macos first, the implementation holds sorted order), quiesce blockers from the 7.5 enum sentence, identity kinds from the 5.5 table row, identify confidence and matched-evidence from the 7.5 identify-session row. Each widening mutant from the verdict battery (partial, assumed, 386, freebsd, other, legacy_alias, guess, guessed) is killed twice: once by the derivation equality, once by an exact-member refusal row through the production entry point.\n20|- FIX (F2): last-element substitution rows for both manifest order loops, first-element-unknown platform row (aix, still sorted-unique so it reaches the vocab check), and first/last missing-registry-key probe rows.\n21|- FIX (F3): NUL-injection fixtures for both SpawnPlan members that reach exec — argv element and env-literal value — via JSON `\\u0000` escapes.\n22|- FIX (F4): identity provider-correlation now pinned with the equal-length claude/gemini pair (both 6), with a length-equality guard so the fixture cannot go blind silently.\n23|- FIX (F5): all ten bound+1 rows plus exactness acceptances on both sides (including the first SP8 fixture on either side: 65537 refused, 65536 accepted). LESSON: a bound+1 mutant is killed only by bound+1 exactly — the first SP8 draft totalled 69,632 bytes, above even the widened bound, and survived. Same class as the token-floor finding: the obligation must carry the literal.\n24|- FIX (F6): aliasing tests for both copy guarantees (`MutationOperations`, `Capabilities`); the quiesce safe-rule comment restated to name backgroundNull as folded into !background by `rawNullableBool` (unreachable, not untested); the vacuous `runner.spawned() != 0` assertion on a Runner never handed to `RequireCapability` removed and re