{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07039-8c36-7981-972e-5e4ed62aa495"},"sequence":707,"recorded_at":1780531400001409,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"58f5c997-17a5-45b9-a711-d639aa7cbef7"},"call_id":"call_01a0703c65f47ff3b3645714b491660f","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3jqsx1/worktree/LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-05\n7|\n8|### 0926 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-6 rework: the vocabulary class closed by census\n9|\n10|- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-5 verdict (changes requested, single blocking finding F1r). Test-only rework: new `internal/provhost/closed_vocabulary_census_test.go`, `requireVocabulary` comparison fix in `closed_vocabularies_test.go`. Production untouched; uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n11|- FIX (F1r): the nine membership-checked vocabularies with no derivation (manifest/probe/capability/identity/identify/quiesce/spawn/status member sets plus the yolo mapping) are now derived from the pinned document — example-JSON keys for 7.3/7.4, first-sentence code spans for the capability-value sentence, TableRowAt Field rows for the 5.5 identity table, per-span member declarations for the 7.5 SpawnPlan/SafeBoundaryProof/ProviderTransactionStatus rows, braced-cell parsing for the identify-session success body, per-row provider-plus-first-flag for the 7.7 table. The census parses production source for package-level []string/map[string]bool/map[string]string with membership use (unknownMember argument, map index, range operand) and requires each of the 19 found vocabularies to carry an executing derivation, in both directions.\n12|- EVIDENCE: probe_widen.json replay, full-package runs, cp+sha256 restores: W1–W9 KILLED (each red three ways — derivation, census subtest, entry-point refusal row), W10/R2/R4 killed, R1/R3 survive as the stated behaviour-preserving bounds. Fail-closed attacks all red: wrong type name, bad cell marker, off-table identity window, unregistered planted vocabulary (`has no registered spec derivation`), blinded string-map scan (`names no production vocabulary`), dropped registration. `requireVocabulary` now uses reflect.DeepEqual, so the V4 joined-member mutant is killed by the derivation alone. Gates: build/vet/GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` 15/15 green, provhost -race green, provhost cover 86.5% unchanged.\n13|- ANOMALY: the capability-value sentence shares its window with the warnings sentence, so a naive span read derives five members including warnings; the derivation truncates to the declaring sentence. The bare 5.5 closed sentence repeats in four sections, so the identity quote carries its schema opener to stay unique. The *Required order lists are excluded from the census by construction (missingMember-only use), which is what keeps R1/R3 surviving.\n14|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n15|\n16|### 0830 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-5 rework: the 28 real survivors, closed by derivation\n17|\n18|- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-4 verdict (changes requested, 106 mutants, 76 killed, 30 survived, 2 stated bounds, 28 real). Test-only rework in `internal/provhost` plus one comment restatement; production untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n19|- FIX (F1, blocking): the eight closed vocabularies the three existing specdoc derivations did not cover are now derived the same way in `internal/provhost/closed_vocabularies_test.go` — probe statuses and evidence from the Section 7.4 sentences, architectures from 7.4 prose cross-checked against the 7.5 probe request row, probe platforms from that row (sorted both sides: the row lists macos first, the implementation holds sorted order), quiesce blockers from the 7.5 enum sentence, identity kinds from the 5.5 table row, identify confidence and matched-evidence from the 7.5 identify-session row. Each widening mutant from the verdict battery (partial, assumed, 386, freebsd, other, legacy_alias, guess, guessed) is killed twice: once by the derivation equality, once by an exact-member refusal row through the production entry point.\n20|- FIX (F2): last-element substitution rows for both manifest order loops, first-element-unknown platform row (aix, still sorted-unique so it reaches the vocab check), and first/last missing-registry-key probe rows.\n21|- FIX (F3): NUL-injection fixtures for both SpawnPlan members that reach exec — argv element and env-literal value — via JSON `\\u0000` escapes.\n22|- FIX (F4): identity provider-correlation now pinned with the equal-length claude/gemini pair (both 6), with a length-equality guard so the fixture cannot go blind silently.\n23|- FIX (F5): all ten bound+1 rows plus exactness acceptances on both sides (including the first SP8 fixture on either side: 65537 refused, 65536 accepted). LESSON: a bound+1 mutant is killed only by bound+1 exactly — the first SP8 draft totalled 69,632 bytes, above even the widened bound, and survived. Same class as the token-floor finding: the obligation must carry the literal.\n24|- FIX (F6): aliasing tests for both copy guarantees (`MutationOperations`, `Capabilities`); the quiesce safe-rule comment restated to name backgroundNull as folded into !background by `rawNullableBool` (unreachable, not untested); the vacuous `runner.spawned() != 0` assertion on a Runner never handed to `RequireCapability` removed and restated as structural.\n25|- BONUS: the manifest digit-first provider-id row also kills MA8, which the verdict battery listed as killed but is now pinned at the manifest layer too.\n26|- ANOMALY: the first NUL-row draft wrote raw NUL bytes into the Go source (binary file, invalid-JSON refusal instead of the NUL arm); replaced with `\\u0000` escapes and verified zero NUL bytes remain. S1's ExecRunner fork/exec flake reappeared in 2 of ~30 full-package mutant runs; every affected mutant also failed its targeted test, so no verdict rests on it.\n27|- EVIDENCE: 29-mutant replay (the 28 real survivors plus MA8) with the reviewer's own harness and spec files: 29 killed, 0 survived. `go build`, `go vet`, `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 15/15 green, provhost `-race` green, provhost cover 86.4% → 86.5%.\n28|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n29|\n30|### 0510 — Provider conformance-harness leaf: operation decoders, derived complements, inventory census 60 → 162\n31|\n32|- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti (final leaf of STORY-260830-3jqsx1). New `internal/provhost` operation layer: manifest (7.3), probe + capability gate (7.4/8.3), profile mapping (7.7), quiescence proof (7.6), SpawnPlan for launch/resume, Provider Identity Record + identify result (5.5), and the single `(operation, operation_id)` key (7.5), with Host.Call conformance sequences (manifest/probe/resume/identify/quiesce end to end, 21 fail-closed capability-by-status tuples with zero processes started, byte-identical lost-prepare retry, changed-body `idempotency_mismatch` passthrough, child-code passthrough table). Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n33|- MECHANISM (leaf-2 item closed here): the derived refusal-arm inventory parses production AST — every `&frameFault` literal, every literal `integrity(...)` argument (with the `decodeStrictObject`-fault wrapper expanded over the derived frame detail set), every `parseMajor` rejection branch keyed by enclosing condition, and every literal first argument to the six refusal constructors — and checks both directions (every derived arm witnessed, every witness derived) plus a census floor. This leaf raised the floor 60 → 162 and added 102 witnesses, one per new arm.\n34|- BLIND SHAPES (stated, not fixed): a one-line wrapper fronting a constructor and an aliased constructor at an unexercised site are both invisible to the arm walk and the site audit; both measured empty in this tree and neither shape was introduced. The file header's \"non-literal shapes never silent\" line was corrected: constructor non-literals are fault conduits by design, not obligations.\n35|- CENSUS-FLOOR REASONING: the floor catches a silently truncated scan (empty, single-file, or short derivation fails even when every surviving arm is witnessed); the reverse witness check catches a deleted or narrowed production branch by orphaning its witness. Raising is routine with new refusals; lowering requires saying why.\n36|- DEFECT (caught by the new tests, fixed before review): the first `DecodeQuiesceProof` draft omitted both open counts from the safe-rule disjunction — `safe:true` with `open_child_count:1` validated. The per-conjunct safe-lie fixtures (one violated fact each) caught it; counts now return through `checkQuiesceCounts` into the rule.\n37|- COMPLEMENTS, NOT SAMPLES: 6 providers × 2 profiles swept; 4 statuses × 2 enabled swept for the probe rule, the pure gate, and one capability key, plus a per-key sweep over all 7 registry keys; keyed operations derived per-row from the Section 7.5 table (capture, materialize, commit, rollback, fork) with the 10 unkeyed operations refused in the same test; registries (operations, capabilities, platforms) re-derived from the Section 7.3 example.\n38|- EVIDENCE: 26 narrowing mutants (order-skip-first, bound+1, grammar weakening, gate `&&`→`||`, disjunct drops, key widening, registry deletion), each presence-asserted, full-package run, cp-aside restore byte-verified, tree hash equal before/after: 24 killed on first run, 2 survived (order checks skipping index 0 — no fixture distinguished the first element), both killed after adding first-element-substitution fixtures. Final: 26/26, 0 survivors. `go test ./...` exit 0, `-race` on provhost exit 0, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 unchanged (17/403, 74 cases — no ownership bindings added or claimed). provhost cover 86.4% (was 88.1%: the new decoders add the same constructor-error propagation branches the audit already records as the uncovered remainder).\n39|- BOUNDS (unchanged and restated): `provhost` still has no importers and imports no new package; no top-level `cmd/`; the ten leaf-2 survivors stay as stated (S11/S12/S13/U2 included — no test implies detached-descendant knowledge); S1's one-off ExecRunner fork/exec red stands recorded. New bounds: mutation receipts live in the transaction document/plugin (host holds no cache — cross-crash durability is the document's property); Section 8 cell values are evidence labels (host pins the fail-closed direction per tuple, not per cell); Section 8.2 store exclusions, commit/rollback result vocabularies, and remaining Section 7.5 request bodies are still opaque; literal secrecy and shell-string argv rules are structural, not content-admitted; record_id is shape-checked, not recomputed.\n40|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n41|\n42|### 0435 — Provider JSONL host leaf round-2 rework: arm identity, exact bounds, production-site pins\n43|\n44|- SCOPE: TASK-260830-qcosxq round-1 verdict (changes requested, 44/66 killed, 18 real survivors). Test-only rework in `internal/provhost` plus README/LOGBOOK honesty items; production untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n45|- FIX (F25, structural, first): every refusal row now names its arm — `requireFrameRefusal` (code + `member` detail + rule detail + non-retryable) for frame refusals, `requireLocalRefusal` (code + rule detail + non-retryable) for invalid_config/integrity/timeout/process arms, plus `observed`-version assertions on both mismatch paths and `status_state` on un